# Line endings. Git stores every text file with LF in the index and leaves the
# working copy to core.autocrlf, so a Windows checkout keeps CRLF on disk and
# adding this file rewrites nothing. The index is already entirely LF, which is
# what makes this safe to introduce at this point.
* text=auto

# CRLF breaks a shebang, so these keep LF everywhere.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Never converted, never diffed. An end-of-line conversion inside a binary file
# corrupts it silently, and nothing in a diff would say so.
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
